      <h3>1. Direct Math Rule</h3>
      <p>Subtract 8 hours from any IDT time. If the result is negative, add 24 to get the EST hour and move back one day on the calendar.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>2. Late Afternoon Overlap Window</h3>
      <p>The standard business overlap occurs between 4:00 PM and 7:00 PM IDT, aligning with 8:00 AM to 11:00 AM EST on the US East Coast.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>3. Seasonal EDT & IDT Alignment</h3>
      <p>When the US enters EDT (UTC-4) and Israel enters IDT (UTC+3), the relative difference between local Tel Aviv and New York clocks becomes 7 hours.</p>
    </article>
